# Context

Update your forecast based after reviewing these forecasts from other superforecasters.

<%- peer_forecasts = @forecasts.reject { |f| f == @forecast } -%>
<%- begin -%>
  <%- case question.type -%>
  <%- when 'binary' -%>
    <%- peer_values = peer_forecasts.map { |f| (f.probability * 100).round(1) }.sort -%>
    <%- own_value = "#{(@forecast.probability * 100).round(1)}%" -%>
    <%- summary = "Your estimate: #{own_value} | Peers — min: #{peer_values.first}%, median: #{peer_values[peer_values.size / 2]}%, max: #{peer_values.last}%" -%>
  <%- when 'numeric', 'discrete' -%>
    <%- peer_values = peer_forecasts.map { |f| f.percentiles[50] }.sort -%>
    <%- own_value = @forecast.percentiles[50] -%>
    <%- summary = "Your P50: #{own_value} | Peers P50 — min: #{peer_values.first}, median: #{peer_values[peer_values.size / 2]}, max: #{peer_values.last}" -%>
  <%- end -%>
<%- rescue StandardError -%>
  <%- summary = nil -%>
<%- end -%>
<%- if summary -%>
# Forecast Summary

<%= summary %>

<%- end -%>
<forecasts>
<%- @forecasts.each do |f| -%>
<%- next if f == @forecast -%>
<forecast>
<%= f.stripped_content('think', 'reflect') %>
</forecast>
<%- end -%>
</forecasts>

# Instructions

- Compare your initial forecast to each of these forecasts, identifying the largest differences and root causes.
- Revise your forecast only if another forecaster presents evidence or a reasoning argument you had not considered. Do not converge toward the group median under social pressure — if your reasoning holds, maintain your position and explain why.
- Provide a revised forecast, include your confidence level and note any uncertainties impacting your revision.
